{"name":"Vampiric Council","hex":"#5c0c0c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vampiric","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the traits of a vampire."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A vampire or vampire-like creature."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vampiric"},{"term":"council","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A committee that leads or governs (e.g. city council, student council).\n\n A local authority.","A local authority."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To sit in council with; to hold discussions with."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/council"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vampire","blocks":[{"text":"A vampire is a mythical creature with a human-like appearance that subsists by feeding on the vital essence of humans. In European folklore, vampires are undead humanoid creatures that visit loved ones and cause mischief or deaths in the neighbourhoods they inhabited while they were alive. They wear shrouds and are often described as bloated and of ruddy or dark countenance, contrasting with the modern gaunt, pale vampire which dates from the early 19th century."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Philip_Burne-Jones_-_The_Vampire.jpg/330px-Philip_Burne-Jones_-_The_Vampire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire"},{"title":"Council","blocks":[{"text":"A council is a group of people who come together to consult, deliberate, or make decisions. A council may function as a legislature, especially at a town, city or county/shire level, but most legislative bodies at the state/provincial or national level are not considered councils. At such levels, there may be no separate executive branch, and the council may effectively represent the entire government. A board of directors might also be denoted as a council."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/GLA_Chamber.jpg/330px-GLA_Chamber.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Council"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Edvard_Munch_-_Vampire_%281895%29_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Edvard_Munch_-_Vampire_%281895%29_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Edvard_Munch_-_Vampire_%281895%29_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/1280px-Edvard_Munch_-_Vampire_%281895%29_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Edvard_Munch_-_Vampire_%281895%29_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Edvard_Munch_-_Vampire_%281895%29_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Vampire (1895) by Edvard Munch","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEdvard_Munch_-_Vampire_(1895)_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/72/Ernst6-thumb.gif/250px-Ernst6-thumb.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/72/Ernst6-thumb.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/72/Ernst6-thumb.gif/250px-Ernst6-thumb.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Illustration of a vampire from Max Ernst's Une Semaine de Bonté (1934)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AErnst6-thumb.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/GarlicBasket.jpg/500px-GarlicBasket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/GarlicBasket.jpg/1280px-GarlicBaske